Subject: [PATCH] passt: accept --ns-mac-addr as the guest MAC address

In passt mode the guest MAC is unknown until the guest sends a frame,
so passt addresses its frames to broadcast. Linux TCP drops segments
whose link-layer destination is not the host (PACKET_HOST), so after
a passt restart an idle guest never answers inbound connections and
never sends anything that would teach passt its address. qrab knows
each guest MAC (it assigns it) and passes it here; passt still
relearns from the guest frames as before.

qrab: work/passt-guest-mac-preset.
---
--- a/conf.c
+++ b/conf.c
@@ -1530,9 +1530,10 @@
 			conf_netns_opt(netns, optarg);
 			break;
 		case 4:
-			if (c->mode != MODE_PASTA)
-				die("--ns-mac-addr is for pasta mode only");
-
+			/* passt: the guest's MAC address, known before its
+			 * first frame, so that a guest that stays silent
+			 * after reconnecting still gets unicast frames
+			 */
 			parse_mac(c->guest_mac, optarg);
 			break;
 		case 5:
--- a/tap.c
+++ b/tap.c
@@ -1486,7 +1486,8 @@
 		 * sends us packets.  Use the broadcast address so that our
 		 * first packets will reach it.
 		 */
-		memset(&c->guest_mac, 0xff, sizeof(c->guest_mac));
+		if (MAC_IS_ZERO(c->guest_mac))
+			memset(&c->guest_mac, 0xff, sizeof(c->guest_mac));
 		break;
 	}
 
